Ex.No:7 Creation of Views, Sequence, Index and Savepoint

Aim
To study and execute SQL commands for creating and using Views, Sequences, Indexes, and Savepoints in a relational database.
Objectives
Create a View to display selected data from one or more tables.
Create and use a Sequence to generate unique numeric values automatically.
Create an Index to improve the speed of data retrieval.
Use SAVEPOINT and ROLLBACK TO SAVEPOINT to control transactions.
Table Creation
CREATE TABLE STUDENT (
    ROLLNO NUMBER(5) PRIMARY KEY,
    NAME VARCHAR2(30),
    DEPARTMENT VARCHAR2(20),
    MARKS NUMBER(3)
);
 Insert Sample Records
INSERT INTO STUDENT VALUES (101, 'ARUN', 'CSE', 85);
INSERT INTO STUDENT VALUES (102, 'PRIYA', 'ECE', 90);
INSERT INTO STUDENT VALUES (103, 'KUMAR', 'CSE', 78);
INSERT INTO STUDENT VALUES (104, 'DIVYA', 'IT', 88);
INSERT INTO STUDENT VALUES (105, 'RAHUL', 'CSE', 92);

COMMIT;
Sample table contents:
